## 3.2 Objective Identity

### Purpose

The Objective Identity section establishes the permanent engineering identity of a System Objective.

Its purpose is to uniquely distinguish every objective within the AVIA repository and provide the foundational information required for governance, traceability, and lifecycle management.

---

### Standard Fields

Every System Objective shall include the following identity fields:

| Field | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| Objective Identifier | Permanent unique identifier (e.g., SO-F-001). |
| Objective Title | Concise engineering title of the objective. |
| Objective Category | Approved engineering category. |
| Objective Type | Classification of the objective where applicable. |
| Baseline Version | Initial approved version of the objective. |
| Current Version | Latest approved version. |
| Lifecycle Status | Current lifecycle stage of the objective. |

---

### Identity Rules

The identity of a System Objective shall:

- Be unique within the repository.
- Remain permanent throughout the objective lifecycle.
- Not be reused after retirement.
- Be independent of implementation details.
- Remain traceable across all approved revisions.

---

### Engineering Note

Changes to the wording or engineering rationale of an objective do not change its identity.

Only approved governance processes may establish a new objective identity.
